Update Linux packages through the system package manager

Firefox hides its update UI in packaged apps because Gecko's updater cannot
write files a package manager owns. Hallow keeps the UI and backs it with
LinuxPackageUpdater (gecko/toolkit/mozapps/update, added by cargo hb prepare):

- AppUpdater runs the package check and install for Linux package installs,
  using the same states, so the About dialog and Settings work unchanged.
- The About dialog's and Settings' restart button also finishes a package
  update.
- Settings shows the update section for package installs, without the
  install-mode choice and Gecko's update history.
- The module and its daily update-timer entry are built on GTK only.

